    "nodeData": {
      "id": "root",
      "topic": "Technology Entity Disambiguation",
      "children": [
        {
          "topic": "Problem",
          "id": "162c467ce1b1f6cd",
          "direction": 0,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "n2",
              "topic": "1. Background",
              "children": [
                {
                  "topic": "processing threat intel reports",
                  "id": "162d95c1e978ebef"
                },
                {
                  "topic": "extract technology/product names",
                  "id": "162d9a480f91708c",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "topic": "match them against what each customer actually runs",
                      "id": "162db6458fb633d3"
                    }
                  ],
                  "expanded": false
                },
                {
                  "topic": "The same technology often appears under many variants",
                  "id": "162dbf36d1b62580",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "topic": "(e.g., \"AWS\", \"Amazon Web Services\", \"AWS Cloud\")",
                      "id": "162dc4c8d59a0cf0"
                    }
                  ],
                  "expanded": false
                },
                {
                  "topic": "Entity disambiguation",
                  "id": "162dc9c96c1fd985",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "topic": "variants to canonical",
                      "id": "162dd3f7eaa27952"
                    }
                  ],
                  "expanded": false
                }
              ],
              "metadata": {
                "source": {
                  "line": 3
                }
              },
              "note": "When processing threat intel reports, we extract technology/product names mentioned in the text so we can match them against what each customer actually runs. The same technology often appears under many variants (e.g., \"AWS\", \"Amazon Web Services\", \"AWS Cloud\"), so we need entity disambiguation: resolving variants to a stable canonical identifier.",
              "direction": 0,
              "style": {
                "fontSize": "20px",
                "borderRadius": "8px",
                "border": "1px solid #888888",
                "background": "#004d65",
                "fontWeight": "bold"
              },
              "branchColor": "#aa7942",
              "expanded": false
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "topic": "2. The Challenge",
              "children": [
                {
                  "topic": "Deterministic solution",
                  "id": "162df18b8c6544bf"
                },
                {
                  "id": "n4",
                  "topic": "All variants → same canonical name",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 13
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "All variants of the same product resolve to the same canonical name."
                },
                {
                  "topic": "Input: arbitrary input string",
                  "id": "162e15f27404cfa7",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "topic": "a technology name extracted from a threat report",
                      "id": "162e1eeb2c440b2a"
                    }
                  ],
                  "expanded": false
                },
                {
                  "id": "n5",
                  "topic": "Different products never collapse to one ID",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 14
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "Different products do not collapse into the same ID (or you have an explicit strategy for handling ambiguity/conflicts)."
                },
                {
                  "id": "n6",
                  "topic": "Output stable across runs, deterministic",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 15
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "The output is stable across runs and independent of non-deterministic components."
                },
                {
                  "topic": "Canonical universe: tens of thousands",
                  "id": "ee6b503a537744b1"
                }
              ],
              "metadata": {
                "source": {
                  "line": 7
                }
              },
              "note": "Design and implement a deterministic entity disambiguation solution for technology names.\n\nGiven an arbitrary input string (a technology name extracted from a threat report), your system should return a stable canonical name such that the three child requirements hold.\n\nAssume the canonical universe is large (tens of thousands).",
              "direction": 0,
              "expanded": false,
              "style": {
                "fontSize": "20px",
                "borderRadius": "8px",
                "border": "1px solid #888888",
                "background": "#004d65",
                "fontWeight": "bold"
              },
              "branchColor": "#aa7942"
            },
            {
              "id": "n7",
              "topic": "3. Scope",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "n8",
                  "topic": "Entity type: technologies / products",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 23
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "Clouds, EDRs, SIEMs, SaaS, libraries; your choice, but be consistent."
                },
                {
                  "id": "n9",
                  "topic": "Canonical name format: your design",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 24
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "E.g., \"AWS EKS\", \"CrowdStrike Falcon\", \"Microsoft Sentinel\". Include rules for casing, punctuation, and vendor/product ordering."
                },
                {
                  "id": "n10",
                  "topic": "Inputs: raw strings only - one name",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 25
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "No additional context from the report needed, unless you define an optional interface."
                },
                {
                  "id": "n11",
                  "topic": "Knowledge source: local KB or dataset",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 26
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "You may use a local dictionary/KB you construct, open datasets, or a small synthetic dataset you include in the repo."
                },
                {
                  "id": "n12",
                  "topic": "Out of scope: UI, ingestion pipelines",
                  "children": [],
                  "metadata": {
                    "source": {
                      "line": 27
                    }
                  },
                  "note": "Building a full UI; production-scale data ingestion pipelines."
                }
              ],
              "metadata": {
                "source": {
                  "line": 19
                }
              },
              "note": "For this exercise, focus on the items below.",
              "direction": 0,
