        {
          "topic": "Brainstorm",
          "id": "e6e00d53d1e849d4",
          "children": [
            {
              "topic": "V2",
              "id": "034878a567981114",
              "note": "Proposal only, nothing moved yet. Same skeleton as the design doc, so Design = copy the ⭐ decisions per section.",
              "style": {
                "fontSize": "24px"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "topic": "0. Inputs & constraints",
                  "id": "4b80ad943489c4f4",
                  "note": "Problem summary, Matan's answers ($1 per ~1M resolves/day, single name, categories for blocking), assumptions.",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "topic": "Matan's answers (22-10-26)",
                      "id": "e6f851a393d083e1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "Categories = your own conceptualization, used to shrink the search space",
                          "id": "38eef6c1ff6c08b5",
                          "note": "Match x only against same-category entities. Input carries no category → we infer it."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Input is one name, may be several words",
                          "id": "2f8385aed201f0e6"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Existing index is fine; a TF-IDF corpus must be built or described",
                          "id": "04a47a149b0e34da",
                          "note": "→ IDF over the aliases themselves."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Anything allowed if cost is reasonable at scale",
                          "id": "e7c506a0745cca53",
                          "note": "Millions of resolves per day per customer for ~$1/day → ~$1 per 1M resolves. No LLM per request."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-32 · Not answered: can input be a vendor alone ('Microsoft')?",
                          "id": "c67ac3aa1eefc466",
                          "note": "Our decision: yes, 'vendor' is a category."
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Measured facts 📊",
                      "id": "0a26400b1eb38e17",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "CPE: 78,261 app vendor:product, 39,316 vendors, 83.5% vendors with 1 product",
                          "id": "97746881a38373c1",
                          "note": "Source: daffainfo/cpelist data/cpes.txt (https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist), downloaded 22-10-26: 192,053 rows, 0 malformed, 53 duplicates. Product-level only (no versions, no titles); includes CPEs seen in CVEs that are not in the official dictionary.\nMethod: keep part 'a' (applications), unique (vendor, product) pairs → 78,261; distinct vendors → 39,316; vendors with exactly one product / all vendors → 83.5%.\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat 'Entity matching assignment questions', 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "20.5% of entities share a product name with another vendor; 'sentinel' exact at 5 vendors",
                          "id": "61df40d7306dee17",
                          "note": "Source: daffainfo/cpelist data/cpes.txt (https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist), downloaded 22-10-26: 192,053 rows, 0 malformed, 53 duplicates. Product-level only (no versions, no titles); includes CPEs seen in CVEs that are not in the official dictionary.\nMethod: group app entities by product slug; a product name used by >1 vendor counts all its entities → 20.5% of 78,261. 'sentinel' as exact product slug appears under 5 vendors (e.g. hashicorp, microfocus, netiq); as a token in 29 entities, none under microsoft.\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat 'Entity matching assignment questions', 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "36.5% of auto-initials (≤4 chars) collide; 'aws' → 6 products, 'ms' → 205",
                          "id": "9fb16d5aa8033b09",
                          "note": "Source: daffainfo/cpelist data/cpes.txt (https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist), downloaded 22-10-26: 192,053 rows, 0 malformed, 53 duplicates. Product-level only (no versions, no titles); includes CPEs seen in CVEs that are not in the official dictionary.\nMethod: for product names with ≥2 tokens (split on _ - .), take first letters; keep initialisms ≤4 chars; collision = initialism mapping to >1 (vendor, product) → 36.5% of distinct initialisms. 'aws' → 6 products, 'ms' → 205.\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat 'Entity matching assignment questions', 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "43% of product names are one token; top tokens: for, server, system, management",
                          "id": "22ae871bdc678f0f",
                          "note": "Source: daffainfo/cpelist data/cpes.txt (https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist), downloaded 22-10-26: 192,053 rows, 0 malformed, 53 duplicates. Product-level only (no versions, no titles); includes CPEs seen in CVEs that are not in the official dictionary.\nMethod: unique product slugs split on _ - .; one-token names / all → ~43%. Token frequency counted once per unique product name (top: for, server, system, management, manager, web, security, enterprise).\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat 'Entity matching assignment questions', 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Vendor dup spellings: 1,386 / 39,316 (3.5%); in-vendor dup products: 566 groups",
                          "id": "5d82b88ba15db115",
                          "note": "Source: daffainfo/cpelist data/cpes.txt (https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist), downloaded 22-10-26: 192,053 rows, 0 malformed, 53 duplicates. Product-level only (no versions, no titles); includes CPEs seen in CVEs that are not in the official dictionary.\nMethod (vendors): lowercase, strip legal/org suffix (inc, corp, corporation, llc, ltd, limited, gmbh, co, company, software, technologies, technology, project, team, foundation, labs, group, systems), drop non-alphanumerics; 1,311 groups with >1 vendor id; removable ids = Σ(size−1) = 1,386 → 3.5% of 39,316. Heuristic, has false merges (linux / linuxfoundation). Compared with Anwar et al. 2020 (~5%).\nMethod (products): same vendor, product slug with non-alphanumerics removed → 566 groups (e.g. saml_single_sign_on / saml_single_sign-on).\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat 'Entity matching assignment questions', 22-10-26. Removable-ids figure re-computed in Computed by Claude (Python) in the chat that built V2, 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "CPE misses: no eks, Okta only as components, Sentinel only as azure_sentinel",
                          "id": "b30eb6ed899ff795",
                          "note": "Source: daffainfo/cpelist data/cpes.txt (https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist), downloaded 22-10-26: 192,053 rows, 0 malformed, 53 duplicates. Product-level only (no versions, no titles); includes CPEs seen in CVEs that are not in the official dictionary.\nMethod: token search in app entities. 'eks' as token: 0 hits. vendor okta: 13 products, all agents/SDKs/components, no 'okta' product. 'sentinel': microsoft only as azure_sentinel. Also vendor split: amazon 107 products vs aws 3.\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat 'Entity matching assignment questions', 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/daffainfo/cpelist"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "KEV names vs CPE: vendor 94%, vendor+product 41%",
                          "id": "041ddfeb7c8fcebc",
                          "note": "Source: CISA KEV known_exploited_vulnerabilities.json from https://github.com/cisagov/kev-data, catalogVersion 2026.10.21: 1,754 CVEs, 738 distinct (vendorProject, product); 703 after dropping 'Multiple Products'. Compared against cpelist (all parts a/o/h).\nMethod: lowercase + drop non-alphanumerics on both sides. Vendor found: 664 / 703 = 94%. Exact vendor+product: 286 / 703 = 41%. Naive slug (spaces → _) gives 32%, so 41% is the fairer number. Misses e.g. Palo Alto Networks / PAN-OS, Apache / Log4j2, Adobe / Experience Manager (AEM) Forms.\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat that built V2, 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/cisagov/kev-data"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "webappanalyzer: cpe on 6.1% of techs → 0.57% of CPE entities",
                          "id": "20b897b9be24ba10",
                          "note": "Source: enthec/webappanalyzer, src/technologies/*.json + categories.json (https://github.com/enthec/webappanalyzer), shallow clone 22-10-26: 7,647 technologies, 109 categories.\nMethod: technologies with a non-empty cpe field / all → 6.1%. Their (vendor, product) from cpe found in the cpelist app set / 78,261 → 0.57%.\nComputed by Claude (Python) in the chat 'Entity matching assignment questions', 22-10-26.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/enthec/webappanalyzer"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false,
                      "note": "Every child note says: source dataset + download date, method, who/where computed. Scripts were run in Claude's sandbox and are not in the repo; re-run before quoting in the design doc."
                    },
