                      "topic": "Papers & standards",
                      "id": "4068279a48d0ae63",
                      "note": "Copied from V1 (22-10-26).\n\nAdded by Claude from a literature search. No paper gives an exact spec for raw string → deterministic canonical; these are the pieces that back or sharpen existing decisions. Extraction/NER papers (CPE-Identifier, VulCPE NER, SOMD) skipped: out of scope.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "NIST CPE specs (standard, not paper)",
                          "id": "aae065a95c720d90",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "NISTIR 7695 Naming → canonical format",
                              "id": "f14337f8b0a4ad9f",
                              "note": "Well-Formed Name vendor:product:version; lowercase, _ for space, escaping rules. Ready-made answer for casing/punctuation/ordering rules. → supports slug id vendor/product (Q3).",
                              "hyperLink": "https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ir/7695/final"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "NISTIR 7696 Name Matching → hard negatives",
                              "id": "ec65cce9717b5281",
                              "note": "Per-attribute relations EQUAL / SUBSET / SUPERSET / DISJOINT. Formal frame for 'child never collapses to parent': Amazon Web Services vs AWS EKS = SUPERSET, not EQUAL. → Q7, Decision rules.",
                              "hyperLink": "https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ir/7696/final"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ir/7696/final",
                              "id": "d32e88df2984b9f3"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Cleaning the NVD (Anwar et al. 2020)",
                          "id": "31d05ff595c46485",
                          "note": "Consolidated inconsistent vendor/product names in NVD. Vendor dedup removed ~5% of vendors; acquisitions not handled.",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "Token-sequence equality: internet-explorer = internet explorer",
                              "id": "23e96530f0ec3876",
                              "note": "→ runtime normalization (Q6 mechanical)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Initials vs short name (ie ↔ internet explorer), manually verified",
                              "id": "03c35a513efaec83",
                              "note": "→ backs ✗ no auto-initials, curated table only (Q5)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Edit distance for typos, then manual verify",
                              "id": "85c2d35a85adb83b"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Canonical = name with most CVEs",
                              "id": "cefd5c8dec2effcf",
                              "note": "→ tie-break / tier signal (Q3 tier)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Substring matching dropped: too many false positives",
                              "id": "5637170d092b6990",
                              "note": "→ backs Sentinel ≠ Microsoft Sentinel without extra evidence (Q7 weak alias)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.15074",
                              "id": "f28b54febb4b1bf0"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false,
                          "hyperLink": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.15074"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Sanguino & Uetz 2017: inventory name → CPE",
                          "id": "33ab7c3f55d1f281",
                          "note": "Computers & Security. Closest to 'match against what the customer runs'.",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "Search product with and without vendor token",
                              "id": "c029a5c9df11a0cd",
                              "note": "Some CPE products embed the vendor name. → alias generation (Q5 A)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Levenshtein ≤ 2, justified by deprecated CPE typo fixes",
                              "id": "aff70a23082607d6",
                              "note": "Higher thresholds produce false matches ('player' ~ 'joomla' at 6). → citable fuzzy guardrail."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Auto top-1 wrong for 2 of 12 → ranked list + human pick",
                              "id": "454f65ba5ce96b5f",
                              "note": "→ backs ambiguous + review queue (Decision rules, Q5 E)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.05347",
                              "id": "459262f00d0fdbb0"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false,
                          "hyperLink": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.05347"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Vajra (IIT Bombay 2024): osquery apps → CPE",
                          "id": "0b4b6e87695f824d",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "Sanitization list",
                              "id": "2235057d658e480d",
                              "note": "Strip Inc/LLC/Corp/Technologies, parentheses, arch + language codes, .app suffix; vendor variants → one name; version → core number. Matches app-plists data."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "fuzz.ratio ≥ 70 → too loose for precision-first",
                              "id": "dc433a5bf2c92b3f",
                              "note": "Use as a counter-example in trade-offs."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.16607",
                              "id": "b052164732bfc6e5"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false,
                          "hyperLink": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.16607"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Scaling: blocking & filtering survey (Papadakis et al.)",
                          "id": "a3b103d7ef15c1e8",
                          "note": "Candidate retrieval at 100k+ canonicals: token blocking, filtering. cpe-guesser = the same idea (inverted word index → vendor:product ranked by frequency). → Scale section, token/IDF index (pipeline step 7).",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.06167",
                              "id": "1321bc9de8c2d59d"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false,
                          "hyperLink": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.06167"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false
