                {
                  "topic": "2. Index model",
                  "id": "24133330397aac1e",
                  "note": "entities, vendors (+hierarchy), categories, aliases, vendor_aliases: fields + invariants.",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "topic": "Tables (source of truth)",
                      "id": "a08e5b7b9062cbf5",
                      "note": "Trees are parent_id columns, no graph DB.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "categories (category_id, parent_id, name)",
                          "id": "54f2b1a248f258c5",
                          "note": "~10 groups, ~40–60 leaves."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "vendors (vendor_id, display_name, parent_vendor_id, relation, since)",
                          "id": "b22649a0689e9530"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "entities (entity_id, vendor_id, product, display_name, category_id, category_source, parent_entity_id, tier, deprecated_by, external_ids{cpe,purl,qid})",
                          "id": "8b4ca4b96aa89a85"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "aliases (alias_norm, entity_id, source, strength, status, added_by, added_at)",
                          "id": "2766883f5f56a5ee"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "vendor_aliases (alias_norm, vendor_id, source, status)",
                          "id": "beb36df4a3e4c4db"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Invariants (checked by validate())",
                      "id": "1c68672f2e0cc7f7",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "Entity ID immutable; rename → alias, merge → redirect",
                          "id": "d96f9262a9ed7763"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Strong alias → exactly one entity; otherwise status=ambiguous with all ids",
                          "id": "09e863b44ea95533"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "No alias makes a child EQUAL to its parent (NISTIR 7696 SUPERSET)",
                          "id": "ca088bffe30217f9"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Vendor tree: no cycles, depth ≤ 3",
                          "id": "d4d902420be8f6fa"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Every entity has a category (uncategorized allowed)",
                          "id": "08f4148b1d5347d6"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Q1. Category taxonomy: what is the closed list?",
                      "id": "ebe33def6fa6260c",
                      "note": "Copied from V1 (22-10-26).\n\nMatan: categories exist to shrink the search space (match x only against same-category entities). The input has no category, so we infer it from keywords or candidates.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "⭐ A. Own closed 2-level list (~10 groups, ~40 leaves) in categories.yaml",
                          "id": "f2fb972e82fe0ea1",
                          "note": "security: edr, siem, firewall, idp/iam, email-sec, vuln-scanner | cloud: cloud-platform, cloud-service | infra: os, database, web-server, container, network-device | dev: library, framework, language, devtool | apps: saas, desktop-app, browser, cms | vendor | uncategorized"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "B. Adopt webappanalyzer (109 cats)",
                          "id": "2429d883bca4593c",
                          "note": "Web/marketing bias, no EDR/SIEM, only 0.57% of CPE entities reachable via its cpe field. Use as a mapping source only.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/enthec/webappanalyzer"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "C. Adopt CNCF landscape tree",
                          "id": "12375cb8e5b61333",
                          "note": "Cloud-native only (CC BY 4.0). Mapping source for container/observability.",
                          "hyperLink": "https://github.com/cncf/landscape"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "D. Wikidata P31/P279 classes",
                          "id": "f9e2d043bcf259fd",
                          "note": "Broad, inconsistent. Mapping source only."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "E. Gartner / G2 categories",
                          "id": "90fbd6856cb69712",
                          "note": "Good security vocabulary but not downloadable/licensed [CONFIRM]. Inspiration for leaf names."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-05 · Flat or tree? → 2 levels (group → leaf)",
                          "id": "ccdd74cccba1f656"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-06 · One category per entity or many? → one primary (+ optional secondary)",
                          "id": "dc36e74c406d361f"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-06 · 'vendor' as a category? → yes, so 'Microsoft' resolves to the vendor",
                          "id": "04c82493e21e19a7"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-06 · Runtime use: block on inferred category; uncategorized is never filtered out",
                          "id": "62c69a737970de51"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Q7. Alias strength & conflict policy",
                      "id": "b4f118143e738d4b",
                      "note": "Copied from V1 (22-10-26).\n\nRow: alias_norm, entity_id, source, strength (strong/weak), status (approved/ambiguous/proposed/rejected).",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "Product-only and ≤3-char aliases → weak",
                          "id": "c0584ed9349407dd"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Alias → >1 entity → ambiguous (keeps all ids) unless manual override",
                          "id": "ef88453fa681fafe"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "A child alias never points to its parent",
                          "id": "ed750c0c0e223b8b"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Source precedence: manual > curated > CPE-derived > external > LLM",
                          "id": "22544c104277abe1"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-27 · Weak but unique alias: resolve with lower confidence (Sentinel → 0.7) or ambiguous?",
                          "id": "54c8b8e51a5646f6"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Q11. Sub-vendors, brands, acquisitions",
                      "id": "d16a8f81f58902ab",
                      "note": "Copied from V1 (22-10-26).\n\nCases where the product's vendor sits under another company. Same pattern for brands and acquisitions.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "Real cases",
                          "id": "650fdd5ba02fbedf",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "AWS ⊂ Amazon",
                              "id": "5210ae2098e361a6",
                              "note": "📊 CPE splits it: vendor amazon (107 products, incl. amazon:aws_lambda) vs vendor aws (3)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Nginx ⊂ F5",
                              "id": "5bb9ce536832b6dd",
                              "note": "📊 webappanalyzer maps Nginx → cpe:2.3:a:f5:nginx. Market still says 'Nginx'."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "SafeNet → Gemalto → Thales",
                              "id": "7cb28bcaff386825",
                              "note": "📊 Acquisition chain in CPE, all with 'sentinel' products."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "NetIQ → Micro Focus",
                              "id": "e57e0296bbcc6baa",
                              "note": "📊 Seen in CPE vendor analysis."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "GitHub ⊂ Microsoft, VMware ⊂ Broadcom, Mandiant ⊂ Google, Red Hat ⊂ IBM",
                              "id": "9a2cc0a238b5396c",
                              "note": "From general knowledge, not checked against CPE."
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Modeling options",
                          "id": "36631b8e5d8a0f50",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ A. vendors.parent_vendor_id + relation",
                              "id": "25bc303be16c28b3",
                              "note": "relation ∈ subsidiary | brand | acquired | division, optional since (date). Tree, depth ≤ 3, no cycles (validate)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "B. Separate brands table (vendor → brands)",
                              "id": "e9473a00add7cc8e",
                              "note": "More tables, same expressiveness. Only if brands need their own attributes."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "✗ C. Collapse to the ultimate parent",
                              "id": "933e60f4c302441a",
                              "note": "'Microsoft GitHub Copilot', 'Broadcom ESXi': loses the names reports actually use, merges unrelated portfolios."
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "⭐ Canonical vendor = the operating brand the market uses",
                          "id": "a56f1df2d33c556b",
                          "note": "AWS EKS (not Amazon EKS), GitHub Copilot, VMware ESXi. Parent appears only in the vendor table."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "⭐ Acquisition never changes the ID",
                          "id": "f3d4148fff875a8e",
                          "note": "vmware/esxi stays. vendor gets a parent; old names stay aliases; 'Broadcom VMware ESXi' comes from parent × product alias rule."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Resolve rules",
                          "id": "e17165efd3c47503",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "Vendor token → own products first, then descendants (confidence penalty)",
                              "id": "f823fcf009011707",
                              "note": "'Amazon EKS' → amazon → descendant aws → AWS EKS ✅"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Never search ancestors' products from a child token",
                              "id": "db9504e36df972d9",
                              "note": "'AWS Alexa' must not resolve to Amazon Alexa."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Own product beats descendant's",
                              "id": "cef0b9b9608a4449",
                              "note": "'Microsoft Copilot' ≠ 'GitHub Copilot'."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Category is not inherited from parent",
                              "id": "6df222292c77fd66",
                              "note": "Amazon retail ≠ AWS cloud."
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-32 · 'AWS' = vendor or the cloud platform?",
                          "id": "47e1289ccd2531a5",
                          "note": "Proposal: two entities, vendor aws and product aws/aws (cloud-platform). A vendor-like input resolves to the flagship platform when one exists; 'Microsoft' (no platform) → vendor entity."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-32 · 'Amazon' vs 'AWS': hard negative?",
                          "id": "b15b25bde4beb002",
                          "note": "Proposal: yes, distinct entities; parent link is metadata, not equality."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Sources for the hierarchy",
                          "id": "4beea691efe5cf5d",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "Wikidata P749 parent organization / P355 subsidiary / P127 owned by",
                              "id": "c271f1f284798a95",
                              "note": "Not queried (blocked here) [CONFIRM]."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "CPE evidence: products filed under another vendor",
                              "id": "0f9c7a183f0a7833",
                              "note": "f5:nginx, amazon:aws_*; dup-vendor groups."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "security-market-map formerNames",
                              "id": "979beceb65a75ce9"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Manual table for tier-1 (~50 rows)",
                              "id": "9ab836dba2194b7c",
                              "note": "The realistic answer for the exercise."
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Q8. Storage shape: source of truth vs runtime",
                      "id": "5d80c5a4b0eb1aed",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "⭐ Source of truth: tables as files in git",
                          "id": "c0ee8551eb779e98",
                          "note": "categories.yaml, vendors.csv, entities.jsonl, aliases.csv, overrides.yaml, mappings/*.csv"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Alternative: one SQLite file as source of truth",
                          "id": "d1c5e26f83e93a5f"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Built snapshot: alias map + vendor map + token/IDF index + entities",
                          "id": "58e8e19fb647d355",
                          "note": "index_version = content hash of the snapshot."
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "↻ → D-42 · One file per vendor (ownership, small diffs) or one big file?",
                          "id": "4245dff7c1775178"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false,
                      "note": "Copied from V1 (22-10-26)."
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Evidence: conflict policy",
                      "id": "1fdab20782a3ddce",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "📄 NISTIR 7696 EQUAL / SUBSET / SUPERSET / DISJOINT → validator rule",
                          "id": "00a483348335c0aa",
                          "note": "Store parent_id; validate() rejects an alias that would make a SUBSET entity EQUAL to its SUPERSET (AWS EKS vs Amazon Web Services).",
