                      ],
                      "expanded": false,
                      "note": "Copied from V1 (22-10-26)."
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Resolve deep-dive (22-10-26)",
                      "id": "a8e7fc1081918739",
                      "note": "Ofek's walk-through: cache/seed, ledger, alias size, hint vs filter, inverted index, scoring, confidence, RAG.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "Q12. Cache vs ledger",
                          "id": "80fecc608f35e3fc",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Two layers: ledger (durable, never evicts) + hot LRU (speed)",
                              "id": "e01c0203311af146",
                              "note": "Ledger = every response ever given, source of truth for same input -> same output. LRU = copy of the hottest ledger rows. A cache alone breaks idempotency: after eviction the answer is recomputed, and if the index changed, so does the answer."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Ledger key = (input_norm, filters, hints, index_version)",
                              "id": "6f4e32cf2d6464d0",
                              "note": "A different hint can give a different answer."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Flow: normalize -> LRU -> ledger -> exact alias -> decompose -> candidates -> score -> decide -> write ledger + LRU",
                              "id": "1b692e3f1ae80338"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "LRU seed strategies",
                              "id": "b5e30eb46da00041",
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "topic": "⭐ A. Ledger top-N by traffic, last 30 days",
                                  "id": "7e3320c61ba5de13"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "B. Aliases of tier-1 entities",
                                  "id": "fd3cc96c269dec97"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "C. Entities seen in last week's threat reports",
                                  "id": "79e6cf907e7085db"
                                }
                              ],
                              "expanded": false
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "↻ → D-30 · LRU size and seed N",
                              "id": "dfcd9fed7d6c9783"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q13. Hint vs filter: two parameter kinds",
                          "id": "0d6c8bb207834149",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ hints = soft: boost matching candidates, never drop others",
                              "id": "4390ff67f65c36c3",
                              "note": "The extractor may guess wrong; the right entity must stay reachable."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ filters = hard: match only within these vendors / categories",
                              "id": "0e9eac239520ae9a",
                              "note": "e.g. a customer's inventory. Nothing left after filtering -> no_match, reason=filtered."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ filters.includeUncategorized defaults to true",
                              "id": "6078446129591abe",
                              "note": "Keeps D-06."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Vendor found inside the input = inferred hint, same path as a caller hint",
                              "id": "7c9fb34d695d5ef4",
                              "note": "Longest-prefix on vendor_aliases: 'CrowdStrike Falcon' -> vendor=crowdstrike, residue=falcon."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "↻ → D-29 · Hint bonus size; does a contradicting hint lower an exact hit's confidence?",
                              "id": "ccad93394c592c8e"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q14. Candidate retrieval: inverted token index",
                          "id": "bde1c5faf2793ecd",
                          "note": "Index from token to the entities containing it, like the index at the back of a book. Lets us score ~20 candidates instead of 300K.",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ One inverted index token -> entity_ids, built offline from all aliases",
                              "id": "1a48709cf9e4a31e",
                              "note": "Includes denormalized vendor-alias x product-alias strings ('aws eks', 'amazon eks'). Runtime = a few lookups, never table joins."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "IDF = log(N / df) over aliases; rare tokens weigh more",
                              "id": "b57e486c0716889e",
                              "note": "'server', 'security', 'cloud' ~ 0 weight."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Typo tokens: char-trigram vocab index -> candidates, Jaro-Winkler verifies",
                              "id": "5ffdecc081b64f38",
                              "note": "crowdstrke -> crowdstrike (JW ~0.98), token weight 0.98."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Union postings -> top-K by IDF overlap -> score",
                              "id": "ed33b919fd5ba3ab"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "↻ → D-26, D-28 · K; trigram / JW thresholds; max typo tokens per input",
                              "id": "0fb0f35321978f2a"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q15. Score & confidence",
                          "id": "57cc2d94e8f2be41",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ score = sum idf(common) / sum idf(union), weighted by token match quality",
                              "id": "9d48a48d2eb64d2f",
                              "note": "Union includes candidate tokens missing from the input -> coverage penalty (AWS EKS vs 'Amazon Web Services')."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Worked example: 'crowdstrke falcon sensor v7.11'",
                              "id": "92ca3fef4debf2e7",
                              "note": "Illustrative IDF crowdstrike 9.1, falcon 7.5, sensor 4.2. E1 CrowdStrike Falcon 0.79, E3 Falcon (Python) 0.36, margin 0.43 -> resolved."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Base by match type: canonical 1.0 > manual alias 0.97 > generated alias 0.9 > fuzzy = score",
                              "id": "05c92c4a23f3e602"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Decide on (s1, margin)",
                              "id": "209e1f1ecdfa5c3a",
                              "note": "s1 >= T_high and margin >= M -> resolved; s1 >= T_low and margin < M -> ambiguous, per-candidate conf = s_i / sum s_topK; else no_match."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Prior (tier, CVE count) is a tie-break only, never decides alone",
                              "id": "ec81dd43d9756835",
                              "note": "'Sentinel' without a hint stays ambiguous."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Calibration table frozen in the snapshot",
                              "id": "782ed64ba892737d",
                              "note": "Fit offline on the dev set so 0.9 ~ 90% precision."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "↻ → D-28 · Values of T_high, T_low, M",
                              "id": "8950fdbc3ebc983e",
                              "note": "After the gold set exists."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "↻ → D-40 · Calibration method: isotonic vs bucket table",
                              "id": "7916e4b0841b0b26"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q16. RAG / embeddings?",
                          "id": "c4c0308bc41811ff",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "✗ Runtime RAG / embeddings",
                              "id": "15f3dee6f8f60c0d",
                              "note": "Hard negatives (CrowdStrike Falcon ~ SentinelOne semantically), ANN is approximate, model drift, cost > $1 per 1M."
                            },
