                },
                {
                  "topic": "8. Decisions log (D-01…)",
                  "id": "53b79557ba7fd617",
                  "note": "One line each: decision · why · evidence link. Becomes 'Key decisions & trade-offs'.",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "topic": "D-01 ⭐ Dictionary-first, deterministic; no LLM / embeddings per request",
                      "id": "35aae0b57135d811",
                      "note": "Why: Budget ~$1 per 1M; Vectorize ~$3.84 per 1M; LLM offline only\nEvidence: 0. Matan, 5. Runtime & cost"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-02 ⭐ CPE is the ID backbone; display names from manual / Wikidata",
                      "id": "c823bcc501317591",
                      "note": "Why: CPE names lag renames (azure_sentinel)\nEvidence: 📊 CPE misses"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-03 ⭐ Creators: CPE + manual + whitelisted (botocore / cloud catalog, endoflife.date); others enrich only",
                      "id": "c2337b891bb63ff0",
                      "note": "Why: Cloud/SaaS missing in CPE; uncontrolled creators = duplicates\nEvidence: Q3"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-04 ⭐ Cross-source merge only on hard IDs; similarity → review",
                      "id": "a998ca282d4f4c01",
                      "note": "Why: Normalization false merges (linux / linuxfoundation)\nEvidence: Q4, 📄 Anwar"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-05 ⭐ Own 2-level category list; security group from security-market-map; mapping tables from others",
                      "id": "1ce4fba00f620beb",
                      "note": "Why: No single source fits; webappanalyzer covers 0.57%\nEvidence: Q1, Security search"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-06 ⭐ One primary category; 'vendor' is a category; uncategorized never filtered out",
                      "id": "a7cf0cc23f68f339",
                      "note": "Why: Blocking must not lose recall\nEvidence: Q1"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-07 ⭐ Runtime normalization is mechanical; semantic variants are built as aliases",
                      "id": "f56b201f7f5e01e4",
                      "note": "Why: Every variant is reviewable before it ships\nEvidence: Q6"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-08 ⭐ No auto-initials; curated acronym table",
                      "id": "b65cfcc944eb1e90",
                      "note": "Why: 36.5% collide; 📄 Anwar verified manually\nEvidence: Q5"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-09 ⭐ Product-only and ≤3-char aliases are weak; alias → >1 entity = ambiguous",
                      "id": "33a53c4cae28dccb",
                      "note": "Why: 20.5% product-name collisions; 📄 Anwar dropped substring match\nEvidence: Q7"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-10 ⭐ Child never equals parent: parent_id + validator",
                      "id": "d9d151d460fc0c17",
                      "note": "Why: NISTIR 7696 SUPERSET; hard negatives in the brief\nEvidence: Q7"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-11 ⭐ Canonical vendor = operating brand; parent_vendor_id; IDs survive acquisitions",
                      "id": "eb883dc195d635c1",
                      "note": "Why: AWS EKS, Nginx/F5, VMware/Broadcom\nEvidence: Q11"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-12 ⭐ Source of truth = files in git; snapshot = SQLite / in-memory, index_version = hash",
                      "id": "dc4d16db146f93a9",
                      "note": "Why: Reviewable diffs, reproducible results\nEvidence: Q8"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-13 ⭐ Updates via git + CLI, PR = review; changesets carry provenance",
                      "id": "973a7161b045a17f",
                      "note": "Why: Fits 3–4h and the update-flow deliverable\nEvidence: Q9"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-14 ⭐ Precision over recall; ambiguity returned with alternatives",
                      "id": "25c740aa438c4d3c",
                      "note": "Why: 📄 Sanguino: auto top-1 wrong 2/12\nEvidence: Decision rules"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-15 ⭐ Fuzzy = IDF token-set + Levenshtein ≤ 2; ≤ 3 chars exact only",
                      "id": "897c42a586d9073b",
                      "note": "Why: 📄 Sanguino threshold; Vajra fuzz 70 too loose\nEvidence: 4. Fuzzy guardrails"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-16 ⭐ Tie-break (score desc, entity_id asc)",
                      "id": "6a0da98ead709579",
                      "note": "Why: Determinism across runs\nEvidence: 4. Decide"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-17 ⭐ Ledger = durable record of every response; hot LRU above it, seeded from ledger top-N",
                      "id": "cca3f9c87325bbb1",
                      "note": "Why: cache eviction breaks idempotency. Key = (input_norm, filters, hints, index_version). Evidence: 4 > Q12"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-18 ⭐ Request carries hints (soft boost) and filters (hard); includeUncategorized default true",
                      "id": "ccbefca96b06b5b6",
                      "note": "Why: extractor hints can be wrong; customer inventory must be a hard scope. Evidence: 4 > Q13"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-19 ⭐ Vendor found in the input = inferred hint, same path as a caller hint",
                      "id": "5500fb7581c3c1e4",
                      "note": "Why: one code path; 'CrowdStrike Falcon' scopes itself. Evidence: 4 > Q13"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-20 ⭐ Candidates from one inverted token index built offline (denormalized vendor x product aliases)",
                      "id": "2fe9314ceebda983",
                      "note": "Why: no runtime joins; O(postings). Evidence: 4 > Q14"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-21 ⭐ Score = IDF-weighted token-set Jaccard with coverage penalty; typos via trigram vocab + Levenshtein <= 2 (↻ D-26)",
                      "id": "ecc888581a7834c2",
                      "note": "Refines D-15. Evidence: 4 > Q15"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-22 ⭐ Decide on (s1, margin); calibration + thresholds frozen in snapshot; prior = tie-break only",
                      "id": "7a33fd88509418b8",
                      "note": "Why: deterministic, calibrated confidence. Evidence: 4 > Q15"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-23 ⭐ No RAG / embeddings at runtime",
                      "id": "49003cabe1f79049",
                      "note": "Why: hard negatives, approximate ANN, cost. Evidence: 4 > Q16"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-24 ⭐ Index enrichment through optional plugins that emit proposals; non-deterministic plugins never run inside build",
                      "id": "92758e14f725b1d1",
                      "note": "Why: LLM help without losing reproducibility or review. Evidence: 3 > Enrichment plugins"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-25 ⭐ Index health is traffic-weighted; priority = traffic x severity",
                      "id": "d82fda9f6c610303",
                      "note": "Why: fix what users hit first. Evidence: 6 > Index health"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-26 ⭐ Typo rule = char-trigram candidates + Levenshtein <= 2 accept; Jaro-Winkler dropped",
                      "id": "19da62248807f341",
                      "note": "Why: one rule, one cited threshold, rapidfuzz one-liner. d<=2 for len>=5, d<=1 for len 4, <=3 chars exact only; token weight = 1 - d/len; max 2 typo tokens per input. Replaces the JW half of D-21; refines D-15. Evidence: 📄 Sanguino (Levenshtein <= 2), 4 > Fuzzy guardrails, 4 > Q14"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-27 ⭐ Base by match type: canonical 1.0 > strong alias 0.97 > generated 0.9 > weak-unique 0.8 > fuzzy = score; weak -> >1 entity = ambiguous",
                      "id": "228ff15d4006dd19",
                      "note": "Why: closes Q7 (weak but unique alias, e.g. EKS) inside the D-22 rule instead of a special branch. 0.8 to calibrate on dev set. Evidence: 2 > Q7, 7 > Test-case bank (EKS)"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-28 ⭐ Initial thresholds: T_high 0.75, T_low 0.5, M 0.15, K 20 (to calibrate on dev set)",
                      "id": "5e23f83eb8e88869",
                      "note": "Why: worked example gives s1 0.79 vs s2 0.36; defaults must exist for the first build. Frozen in the snapshot (D-22). Evidence: 4 > Q15 worked example"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-29 ⭐ Hint bonus = +0.15 additive to candidates matching the hinted vendor/category; exact strong hit ignores hints; a contradicting hint never lowers confidence (to calibrate)",
                      "id": "c0473aa3366e41f8",
                      "note": "Why: hints are soft (D-18); the right entity must stay reachable. Evidence: 4 > Q13"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-30 ⭐ In code: LRU = functools.lru_cache(maxsize=10_000); Ledger = Protocol + in-memory stub. Production: durable ledger, LRU seeded with top-1,000 by 30-day traffic",
                      "id": "8ad503ac4ecb29b9",
                      "note": "Why: the brief needs stability across runs, which a frozen snapshot + pure function already gives; the durable ledger is a production concern -> doc + stub. Ofek chose stub (22-10-26). Evidence: D-17, 4 > Q12, ex.md \"stub out production concerns\""
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-31 ⭐ Ledger policy: key includes index_version, so a new version never conflicts with old rows; replay diff is the gate. Inside one version (overlay) improve-only: no_match -> resolved allowed, a resolved answer never changes",
                      "id": "4ff580147f2dfc65",
                      "note": "Why: merges the two ledger placeholders into one rule that follows from the key. Evidence: Design V2 > 2 Flows, D-17"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-32 ⭐ 'AWS' = two entities: vendor aws (category vendor) + product aws/aws 'AWS' (cloud-platform); vendor-like input resolves to vendors.flagship_entity_id when set, else the vendor entity ('Microsoft'). 'Amazon' != 'AWS' (hard negative)",
                      "id": "22a6694df861b2dd",
                      "note": "Why: test bank needs AWS -> cloud platform and Amazon vs AWS distinct; parent link is metadata, not equality. Evidence: 2 > Q11, 7 > Test-case bank"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-33 ⭐ Display-name precedence manual > Wikidata label > CPE title > prettified slug. Canonical format '<Vendor> <Product>', vendor omitted when the product name already starts with it, symbols kept (C++, .NET), no trailing punctuation. ID = ascii lowercase vendor/product slug (CPE WFN), immutable",
                      "id": "bb322f46590d5059",
                      "note": "Why: ex.md asks for explicit casing / punctuation / ordering rules. Evidence: 2 > Canonical name format, Parking lot"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-34 ⭐ categories.yaml v1 = the 23 leaves of Q1-A (security 6, cloud 2, infra 5, dev 4, apps 4, vendor, uncategorized); coverage target tier-1 100%, long tail may stay uncategorized",
                      "id": "e49a7400c36925ef",
                      "note": "Why: already ⭐ in Q1; freezing the list unblocks the seed file. Evidence: 2 > Q1, D-05, D-06"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-35 ⭐ Runtime storage: one SQLite snapshot file (entities, aliases, postings, idf, thresholds, calibration); exact-alias dict in memory; idx build prints alias count + RSS; >= 1M aliases -> SQLite-backed lookups. Postgres + Bloom = doc only",
                      "id": "0002ada7732be8fd",
                      "note": "Why: one consistent number instead of 100MB vs 600MB; same artifact runs in-process. Python dict for ~1M aliases ≈ 150-250MB [CONFIRM, measure after first build]. Evidence: 2 > Q17, 5 > Scale, 5 > Runtime & cost"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-36 ⭐ Update API: mutations idempotent (upsert keyed by id / alias_norm); provenance = source, actor, added_at (ISO 8601), reason, evidence_url; approver = PR reviewer (CODEOWNERS per vendor file); reload = atomic snapshot swap on index_version change (doc only; code restarts)",
                      "id": "0f8197293a38d379",
                      "note": "Why: closes the four ⏳ in Update API with the git + CLI model of D-13. Evidence: 5 > Q9"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-37 ⭐ Plugins = doc only + Port stub in code. Auto-approve only for deterministic plugins that pass validate() and the eval gate; everything else -> review. Proposal file proposals/<plugin_id>/<YYYY-MM-DD>.jsonl. LLM plugins pin model + prompt hash in the manifest; cost cap $5 per run (to calibrate)",
                      "id": "098c2e594f92ce0b",
                      "note": "Why: keeps D-24 without build time. Evidence: 3 > Enrichment plugins"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-38 ⭐ Gold set in code = test bank (25) + leave-one-out over all aliases + synthetic typos (~200 cases); doc target 300-500 hand-labeled. Targets: precision >= 0.98 on resolved, coverage >= 0.90 (to calibrate)",
                      "id": "72a2dda65abdaf8b",
                      "note": "Why: defaults so the eval harness and the threshold sweep can run on day one. Risk: leave-one-out inflates precision. Evidence: 6 > Testing the formula"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-39 ⭐ Index-health SLOs (doc only): unresolved < 5%, ambiguous < 3%, tier-1 precision >= 99%, source age <= 30 days, p99 < 5 ms in-process, cost <= $1 per 1M (to calibrate)",
                      "id": "9993b0b4fd5267b0",
                      "note": "Why: D-25 needs numbers for the doc. Evidence: 6 > Index health metrics"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-40 ⭐ Calibration = bucket table (10 bins, monotone) fitted on the dev set and frozen in the snapshot; isotonic regression = doc only",
                      "id": "1673db9ecf454ad1",
                      "note": "Why: simple, deterministic, no sklearn. Evidence: 4 > Q15"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-41 ⭐ CPE parts a + o; deprecatedBy -> alias of the replacement; dup spellings -> review; tier = manual 1 / 2 / 3 (default 3), long tail kept as tier-3; 'MS' in vendor_aliases valid only with a product residue",
                      "id": "2179316ea5fde617",
                      "note": "Why: all were already answered with → in the parking lot; now recorded. Evidence: 9 > Open decisions (Q1-Q11)"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-42 ⭐ Code: one file per table (categories.yaml, vendors.csv, entities.jsonl, aliases.csv); per-vendor file split = doc only (maintainability at 100k+)",
                      "id": "67424f1ce866d33c",
                      "note": "Why: a 300-entity seed does not need per-vendor files. Evidence: 2 > Q8"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-43 ⭐ Scope for 3-4h: code = Flow A (build) + Flow B (resolve) + CLI (build / validate / resolve / eval / add-alias) + tests + Makefile + Dockerfile. Stubs in code (Protocol + comments): ledger, monitoring, review queue, plugin port. Doc only: Flow D, index health, REST, Wikidata / purl / Repology joins",
                      "id": "51ed0e06797fe6ba",
                      "note": "Why: ex.md says stub out production concerns; Design V2 > 10 did not fit the time budget. Ofek confirmed ledger stub; Flow D doc only by default (22-10-26). Evidence: ex.md Deliverables, 0 > Q10"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-44 ⭐ Runtime never walks the vendor tree or infers category: build emits denormalized aliases parent-vendor x product and category-label x product (strength = generated). Runtime decompose = vendor longest-prefix only",
                      "id": "a43bd0b5a80244a6",
                      "note": "Why: 'Amazon EKS' and 'Sentinel SIEM' pass with one code path; D-20 already denormalizes vendor x product. Evidence: 2 > Q11 Resolve rules, 4 > Q14"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-45 ⭐ Reproducible environment: Makefile (make setup / test / resolve NAME=...) + Dockerfile python:3.12-slim",
                      "id": "0d29d8c7228d3ac3",
                      "note": "Why: a deliverable in ex.md with no node in Design V2. Evidence: ex.md Reproducible Environment"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-46 ⭐ Implementation = Python 3.12: pytest + hypothesis, rapidfuzz, sqlite3 stdlib, Pydantic at file boundaries",
                      "id": "c3fd558b1a9d1a12",
                      "note": "Why: sqlite3 and Levenshtein come for free; data-processing fits the Python stack. Rejected: Node 22 + TypeScript + Zod. Ofek chose Python (22-10-26). Evidence: 0 > Inputs"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "D-47 ⭐ Unknown input default: status = no_match, canonical_name = null, confidence = 0, queued for review. Assumption for the doc: closed world, runtime never mints IDs; unknowns become canonicals only through Flow C. [WAITING ON MATAN]",
                      "id": "a5455ebb17411400",
                      "note": "Why: keeps the index closed and reviewable; a provisional ID would need a merge path. Question to Matan: \"When the resolver cannot match an input to any catalog entity, do you want no_match (null + review queue) or a provisional canonical ID (e.g. unresolved/<slug>) that gets merged later?\" Evidence: 1 > Approach, D-14"
                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Approach: dictionary-first, deterministic",
                      "id": "ff6dbe3f29b9e17f",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "Exact alias lookup after normalization",
                          "id": "374a5932de292718"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Fuzzy fallback only with strict guardrails",
                          "id": "861a2798fa5b4012"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "No LLM in the resolve path",
                          "id": "5cae9e6f45d57dec"
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "LLM offline only, to propose aliases for review",
                          "id": "57492bbfa0ab4021"
                        }
                      ],
                      "expanded": false,
                      "note": "Copied from Design V1."
                    },
