                    },
                    {
                      "topic": "Index Build: Questions & Options (22-10-26)",
                      "id": "e1cb6efe63380124",
                      "note": "Added by Claude from the conversations: Matan's answers, CPE analysis (78,261 app vendor:product, 20.5% product-name collisions, 36.5% auto-initials collide), source research. ⭐ = recommended option, ❓ = open decision.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "topic": "Build pipeline (order)",
                          "id": "5897e6eaf6f9da43",
                          "note": "The questions below follow this order.",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "1. Ingest sources (raw, pinned versions)",
                              "id": "1bf6750554656993"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "2. Create canonicals (creator sources only)",
                              "id": "0421c43d3671f453"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "3. Merge / dedup across sources (hard IDs)",
                              "id": "704008e4be5754a0"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "4. Assign category",
                              "id": "8eea7eb837b8a025"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "5. Generate + join aliases",
                              "id": "af936c8983a6178c"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "6. Validate conflicts",
                              "id": "42f9b5cd2baed968"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "7. Build token / IDF index",
                              "id": "48ab5a28d792c36e"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "8. Eval gate",
                              "id": "5ec4eae2ec5cbf95"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "9. Publish snapshot + index_version",
                              "id": "69513c2a812cff6b"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q1. Category taxonomy: what is the closed list?",
                          "id": "e9c238b5098ef6dc",
                          "note": "Matan: categories exist to shrink the search space (match x only against same-category entities). The input has no category, so we infer it from keywords or candidates.",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ A. Own closed 2-level list (~10 groups, ~40 leaves) in categories.yaml",
                              "id": "93b35ed701e86475",
                              "note": "security: edr, siem, firewall, idp/iam, email-sec, vuln-scanner | cloud: cloud-platform, cloud-service | infra: os, database, web-server, container, network-device | dev: library, framework, language, devtool | apps: saas, desktop-app, browser, cms | vendor | uncategorized"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "B. Adopt webappanalyzer (109 cats)",
                              "id": "cbc7887e2532f8c4",
                              "note": "Web/marketing bias, no EDR/SIEM, only 0.57% of CPE entities reachable via its cpe field. Use as a mapping source only.",
                              "hyperLink": "https://github.com/enthec/webappanalyzer"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "C. Adopt CNCF landscape tree",
                              "id": "2f7b36c4c3762cb1",
                              "note": "Cloud-native only (CC BY 4.0). Mapping source for container/observability.",
                              "hyperLink": "https://github.com/cncf/landscape"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "D. Wikidata P31/P279 classes",
                              "id": "d016e452b0cd0e81",
                              "note": "Broad, inconsistent. Mapping source only."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "E. Gartner / G2 categories",
                              "id": "12a59c0e3046dbc6",
                              "note": "Good security vocabulary but not downloadable/licensed [CONFIRM]. Inspiration for leaf names."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Flat or tree? → 2 levels (group → leaf)",
                              "id": "9ae5ac6ab303ceeb"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ One category per entity or many? → one primary (+ optional secondary)",
                              "id": "dd5151cebbcb4916"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ 'vendor' as a category? → yes, so 'Microsoft' resolves to the vendor",
                              "id": "9a009a967dfa4fdb"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Runtime use: block on inferred category; uncategorized is never filtered out",
                              "id": "ac68d5a48625bbfa"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q2. How does each canonical get its category?",
                          "id": "2084533cd5d74c53",
                          "note": "Precedence order, highest first. Store category_source on the entity.",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "1. Manual file (tier-1)",
                              "id": "ce2db6048051bc3a"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "2. Mapping tables: source category → our category",
                              "id": "ed15fee1d67772aa",
                              "note": "webappanalyzer cats, endoflife.date category (os/db/framework/server-app/lang), cloud-catalog tags, CNCF. Joined to the entity by hard ID (cpe)."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "3. Wikidata P31 → our category map",
                              "id": "75e672194fe5b4eb"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "4. Keyword rules on CPE product/title",
                              "id": "d2db585b85064c62",
                              "note": "antivirus, firewall, siem, _sdk, plugin, server..."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "5. Vendor default (weak)",
                              "id": "cf163634b16a5eee",
                              "note": "e.g. crowdstrike → security group."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "6. LLM offline for top-N → review",
                              "id": "fd121f0888d945e9"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "7. Default: uncategorized",
                              "id": "e990e23b88d93984"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Coverage target? → tier-1 ~100%, long tail may stay uncategorized",
                              "id": "f0705537a6856153"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q3. Which sources may CREATE canonicals (vs enrich only)?",
                          "id": "0029d7981492fe31",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "A. Closed world: CPE + manual file only",
                              "id": "cca6899571e93f4b"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ B. CPE + manual + whitelisted creators",
                              "id": "a5f9084a43139f4c",
                              "note": "Whitelisted: cloud catalog (AWS/Azure/GCP services), endoflife.date. Every new entity is deduped against CPE first. Everything else only adds aliases/attributes."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "C. Any source creates, dedup by similarity",
                              "id": "41a34122e9a3c002",
                              "note": "Too noisy, non-reviewable at scale."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Which CPE parts? → a + o (Windows, FortiOS are 'o'), h optional",
                              "id": "25dfb6c1d687c96a"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Deprecated CPE (deprecatedBy) → alias of the replacement, not an entity",
                              "id": "c8c2ef856ea77934"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Dup spellings inside CPE (566 groups, aws_lambda / aws-lambda) → merge via review",
                              "id": "3872cb626fb9e0ac"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Tier per entity: how ranked?",
                              "id": "a083bed316f04096",
                              "note": "manual tier-1, has Wikidata QID, CVE count. Used for tie-break and to choose who gets LLM aliasing."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Long tail (CMS plugins etc.): keep as tier-3 or drop?",
                              "id": "c849732533cb2ce9"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ ID scheme: vendor/product slug, immutable; rename → alias; merge → redirect",
                              "id": "99ce24e0c2937597"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Display name: manual > Wikidata label > CPE title > prettified slug",
                              "id": "5597cff06570cfc4"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q4. How to merge across sources (build-time)?",
                          "id": "8db8c49bcc236eaa",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Auto-join only on hard IDs",
                              "id": "267bc0b99efd7008",
                              "note": "cpe, purl (purl2cpe), Wikidata QID, cpe field in webappanalyzer / endoflife.date."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Name-similarity matches → review queue, never auto",
                              "id": "69c94f351b0a0cc5"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Vendor dedup: suggest + review",
                              "id": "b9a3ef725b43291d",
                              "note": "1,311 candidate groups after suffix normalization, with false merges (linux / linuxfoundation). Keep vendor_aliases + parent_vendor_id (SafeNet → Gemalto → Thales)."
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q5. Alias sources: where from, by yield / effort",
                          "id": "df132c3d02357d4f",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ A. Generated by rules from the entity (free, deterministic)",
                              "id": "67f263e933e28947",
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "topic": "vendor + product; product only (weak)",
                                  "id": "d60023af3e0c0359"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "CPE slug → words: _ and - → space, decode \\+ \\'",
                                  "id": "c2205f0c3e36a0a9"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "title minus version",
                                  "id": "3bd84175dd133172"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "vendor alias × product: Amazon / AWS × EKS",
                                  "id": "2228825b0ae64d08"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "symbol forms: C++ ↔ cpp, .NET ↔ dotnet, C# ↔ csharp",
                                  "id": "df3cb91868d9759e"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "✗ No auto-initials: 36.5% collide → only from the curated table",
                                  "id": "4a1e93e1f084078d"
                                }
                              ],
                              "expanded": false
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "B. External names joined by hard ID",
                              "id": "9a40c36e69a9cd73",
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "topic": "⭐ Wikidata label + altLabels (en)",
                                  "id": "4c6e1fc5c47d1ab1",
                                  "note": "Best for tier-1, includes acronyms like AWS.",
                                  "hyperLink": "https://www.wikidata.org"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "Package names via purl2cpe (npm, PyPI, Maven)",
                                  "id": "16179318f75863ce",
                                  "hyperLink": "https://github.com/scanoss/purl2cpe"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "Repology project names",
                                  "id": "68bbedfafd115bcf",
                                  "note": "Open-source packages only; DB dumps at dumps.repology.org; data license not stated [CONFIRM].",
                                  "hyperLink": "https://repology.org"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "Homebrew casks / winget Publisher.Package",
                                  "id": "f9edc60823adec6f",
                                  "hyperLink": "https://github.com/Homebrew/homebrew-cask"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "Cloud catalog long + short names",
                                  "id": "937606d8f41c8fbb",
                                  "note": "\"Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service\" / \"EKS\""
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "webappanalyzer names, endoflife.date titles",
                                  "id": "7fa8171b7515e967",
                                  "hyperLink": "https://github.com/enthec/webappanalyzer"
                                },
                                {
                                  "topic": "Old CPE names: azure_sentinel → Microsoft Sentinel",
                                  "id": "c9b03f56350a4db6"
                                }
                              ],
                              "expanded": false
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ C. Small curated tables (high value)",
                              "id": "ef22bc641e04af11",
                              "note": "Acronyms (AWS, GCP, MS, K8s, M365), vendor prefixes, rename history."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "D. LLM offline proposals, top-N tier-1 only → review",
                              "id": "3d7cffc5ca53b7cf"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "E. Feedback loop: unresolved / ambiguous queue → reviewer adds alias",
                              "id": "079c690c97e2e32a"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ In code: A + C + small B sample; doc: the rest",
                              "id": "473702849b782487"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q6. Acronyms & expansions: build-time or runtime?",
                          "id": "862a63872adb7f86",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Build-time: every expansion becomes an alias row, conflict-checked",
                              "id": "b4827f7eee4bed53"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Runtime: mechanical only",
                              "id": "dfff0bb0dc8c2606",
                              "note": "NFKC, lowercase, whitespace, symbol table, version strip. No noise-word drop, no acronym expansion."
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Acronym sources: curated table + Wikidata altLabels + cloud short names",
                              "id": "13c74bcd01e4879c"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ 'MS Sentinel': MS → Microsoft via vendor_aliases, valid only with a product",
                              "id": "03df9cc70ccde8d6"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q7. Alias strength & conflict policy",
                          "id": "761973eec9916778",
                          "note": "Row: alias_norm, entity_id, source, strength (strong/weak), status (approved/ambiguous/proposed/rejected).",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "Product-only and ≤3-char aliases → weak",
                              "id": "398a459ff66110c6"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Alias → >1 entity → ambiguous (keeps all ids) unless manual override",
                              "id": "6769a6d3ce83f217"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "A child alias never points to its parent",
                              "id": "858aae71925dba25"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Source precedence: manual > curated > CPE-derived > external > LLM",
                              "id": "1fcfc25548019b4d"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "❓ Weak but unique alias: resolve with lower confidence (Sentinel → 0.7) or ambiguous?",
                              "id": "e99dda32fe352410"
                            }
                          ],
                          "expanded": false
                        },
                        {
                          "topic": "Q8. Storage shape: source of truth vs runtime",
                          "id": "3ec22b35f6ce38a5",
                          "style": {
                            "fontSize": "20px"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "topic": "⭐ Source of truth: tables as files in git",
                              "id": "81035b8f8c50e81a",
                              "note": "categories.yaml, vendors.csv, entities.jsonl, aliases.csv, overrides.yaml, mappings/*.csv"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Alternative: one SQLite file as source of truth",
                              "id": "1d4816d1d41fcea6"
                            },
                            {
                              "topic": "Built snapshot: alias map + vendor map + token/IDF index + entities",
                              "id": "e54a65f6a04a79e6",
